Roy Kidder <RoyKidder@remove-this-part.yahoo.com> wrote:
> On Wed, 17 Mar 2004 02:02:47 +0100, M�ns Rullg�rd wrote:
> 
>> Most of them will run if the kernel has ECOFF support enabled and you
>> install the tru64 shared libraries.
> 
> I copied the binary over and ran in only to get the error message: "Fatal
> Error: cannot map libpthread.so". libpthread.so does exist in
> /usr/lib/libpthread.so,

This is NOT THAT library.  Tru64 shared libs will be located in places
like /shlib and /usr/shlib, have their own loader, and a format quite a
bit different than /usr/lib/libpthread.so which is a Linux library.  If
you do not have corresponding pieces installed then none of shared Tru64
libraries will be found.

Also Tru64 programs using threading will have problems on Linux.  Saying
that on a number of occasions I got such things to run correctly by
"cheating" and making 'libpthread.so' into a link to libc.so, IIRC; of
course in /usr/shlib and not with Linux libraries.  Surprisingly enough
quite often this is all what you need.

   Michal


